specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-634-```text
--
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-643-Round N:  Model streams final text with stopReason "end_turn"
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-644-          Server commits all open entries
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:645:          Server sends stream_end
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-646-```
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-647-
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:648:The client observes this as a sequence of `entry_upsert`, `entry_delta`, and `entry_commit` messages, terminated by a `stream_end`. The tool loop is transparent to the client -- it does not need to track rounds.
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md-649-
