specs/hal-engine-thinking-tag-parser/spec.md:8:A model wraps its internal reasoning in `<thinking>...</thinking>`, and that text arrives split across streaming chunks at arbitrary offsets. A tag can be cut in half — `<think` ending one chunk and `ing>` opening the next — so a parser deciding chunk by chunk will either leak half a tag into user-facing text or swallow a bracket that was never a tag at all. `ThinkingTagParser` is the stateful buffer that makes chunk boundaries invisible: it holds back only what could still grow into a tag, and emits everything else at once so streaming stays responsive.
